    "created_at": "2015-08-06T11:13:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-06T11:13:50Z",
    "body": "And the way HTML patches this assumes a notification system rather than a lazy approach. While the difference is not observable, specifying it in the lazy way would avoid people suggesting custom element callbacks for it, for instance. So yes, both HTML and URL need changes.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
